{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And it shall be, if the wicked one be a son of the blow</b> — בן is לשון בינה (understanding), to tell you that he must strike with measured assessment, that they assess him how many lashes he is fit to receive, and that they strike him a number of lashes fit to be tripled (השתלש). And so the words of Agur בן יקה — that he gathered (אגר) understanding and brought it forth. And so Joshua בן נון — who was filled with wisdom and understanding." "<b>And the judge shall cause him to fall</b> — והפילו in gematria is doubled (כפול), teaching that the strap must be doubled." "<b>According to</b> — two times in the Masorah: here, and the other: והשיגה ידו ומצא כדי גאולתו — teaching that he is redeemed and released."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The phrase 'מכות הראויות להשתלש' is obscure; read hyper-literally as 'lashes fit to be tripled.' The argument likely concerns the relationship between the assessment and the tripling mechanism in rabbinic lashings, but the terse phrasing is preserved without interpretation.", 1 "The word והפילו is stated to have a gematria value that is 'doubled' (כפול); the specific numeric value is not given by the author and is not supplied here.", 2 "The second occurrence is Leviticus 25:26 (והשיגה ידו ומצא כדי גאולתו), identified with certainty but not added inline per discipline."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:41.704114956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}